cleanup 0.1.0-dev: reclaim disk space from regenerable dev artifacts, stale git
worktrees and retired tools' leftovers, without deleting work.

Usage: cleanup [OPTIONS] [ROOT]

Runs as a dry run unless -d/--delete is given.

Mode:
  -n, --dry-run              Preview only; delete nothing (default; the last of -n/-d wins)
  -d, --delete               Delete selected items (needs TUI confirmation or -f/--force)
  -f, --force                Skip the TUI and confirmation when deleting

Selection:
  -r, --root DIR             Directory to scan (default ~/Projects)
  -c, --config FILE          Config file merged over the defaults (default ~/.config/cleanup/config.toml)
  -o, --only IDS             Run only these cleaner ids (comma-separated or repeated)
  -x, --exclude IDS          Skip these cleaner ids (comma-separated or repeated)
  -v, --venvs                Python: include marker-verified virtualenvs
  -m, --modules              Node: include node_modules
  -u, --retired IDS          Treat these configured tool ids as retired for this run
  -a, --age DAYS             Minimum idle age for worktrees and retired tools (default from config)

Safety overrides:
  -D, --include-dirty        UNSAFE: also delete git trees with uncommitted changes, untracked files or an unreachable detached HEAD

Output:
  -T, --no-tui               Plain-text output instead of the interactive TUI
  -s, --show-skipped         Show skipped and protected items
  -g, --group-by MODE        Initial TUI grouping: cleaner or project (default cleaner)

Information:
  -l, --list-categories      List cleaners and retired tools, then exit
  -P, --print-config         Print the default config, then exit
  -M, --print-man            Print the man page (roff), then exit
  -h, --help                 Print help, then exit
  -V, --version              Print the version, then exit

Examples:
  cleanup                         Interactive dry run over ~/Projects
  cleanup -d -v -m                Review and delete, including venvs and node_modules
  cleanup -T -d -f -o python,rust Delete Python caches and Rust targets without prompting
  cleanup -u cursor,zed           Preview leftovers of tools you no longer use
  cleanup -P > ~/.config/cleanup/config.toml
  cleanup -M | man -l -

Exit status: 0 success, 1 some deletions failed, 2 usage/config/root error, 130 interrupted.
